Q: How to get max length of a property using Entity Framework Core A: <p><strong>Please find the below-attached code for your reference :</strong></p>
<p>You can access the max length using <code>System.Reflection</code>.</p>
<pre><code> var maxLength = typeof(Customer).GetProperty(nameof(Customer.Street)).GetCustomAttribute&lt;MaxLengthAttribute&gt;().Length;

 Console.WriteLine(maxLength);
</code></pre>
